  Composing an immutable object could look either different or the same when it
  is done as a command to be executed at runtime *vs* when it is done at
  compile time to produce an artifact of computer programming. In the latter
  case, it would be useful to be able to compose different parts of the object
  at different places in the code, similiar to how a class can be "reoopened"
